# Repository Structure

```
[project-root/
├── src/
│   ├── app/              — Next.js App Router (pages + API routes)
│   ├── components/       — React UI components
│   │   └── [Name]/
│   │       ├── index.tsx
│   │       └── [Name].test.tsx
│   ├── services/         — Business logic
│   ├── repositories/     — Database access (Prisma)
│   ├── lib/              — Shared utilities
│   └── types/            — TypeScript type definitions
├── prisma/
│   └── schema.prisma     — Database schema (single file)
├── docs/                 — Project documentation
│   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md
│   └── designs/
├── public/               — Static assets
└── __tests__/            — Integration tests]
```

## Dependency Rules

```
[UI / Pages  →  Services  →  Repositories  →  Types]
                                                 ↑
                              (dependencies flow down only)
```

- [UI must NOT import from repositories directly]
- [Services must NOT import from UI]
- [All database access goes through repositories/]

## Naming Conventions

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase directory + index.tsx | `components/UserCard/index.tsx` |
| Services | camelCase + `.service.ts` | `services/auth.service.ts` |
| Types | camelCase + `.types.ts` | `types/user.types.ts` |
| API routes | lowercase + `route.ts` | `app/api/users/route.ts` |
| Tests | same name + `.test.tsx` | `UserCard.test.tsx` |

## Protected Areas

<!-- Files/directories that should not be modified without explicit approval -->

- [`src/core/`] — Core business rules, changes need review
- [`prisma/schema.prisma`] — Schema changes need migration plan
- [`src/auth/`] — Security-sensitive, requires careful review
